<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Schleswig War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1864">1864</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Danish-Prussian War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> War was fought in 1864 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and the allied German powers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. It began after Denmark adopted a constitution binding Schleswig more closely to the kingdom, contrary to earlier agreements. After defeat at Dybbøl and the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutland">Jutland</a>, Denmark ceded Schleswig, Holstein and Lauenburg by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-vienna-1864">Treaty of Vienna</a>, losing about two-fifths of its territory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-schleswig-war.jpg" alt="Second Schleswig War" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wilhelm Camphausen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1866_Camphausen_Crossing_to_Alsen_anagoria.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
